/run and ! no longer wait for a backgrounded child to die. Committed as e33a79d6; build, all 6398 tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass.

The bug: yoyo run 'sleep 6 & echo hi' took 6.0s even though sh exited at once. run_shell_command in src/commands_run.rs read stdout to the end before waiting on the shell, and the backgrounded sleep was still holding the pipe open.

The fix: stdout and stderr are now read on their own threads while the main path waits on the shell. After the shell exits, the readers get 2s (RUN_READER_GRACE, the same grace the model's bash tool in src/tools.rs uses) to drain. Then /run returns what they read with the real exit code, and prints a dim note that a background process still holds the output.

On the built binary:

| Command | Wall time | Exit |
|---|---|---|
| sleep 6 & echo hi | 2.00s (was 6.0s) | 0 |
| sleep 6 >/dev/null 2>&1 & echo quiet | 0.00s | 0 |
| echo a; sleep 0.3; echo b | 0.30s | 0 |
| exit 3 | 0.00s | 3 |

The redirected job never held the pipe, so it returns at once, as before.

Tests, written first: the three background-child cases failed by name on the old code. The near-miss tests passed on both versions: sequential lines in order, exit 3, and line splitting with \r\n, blank lines and a final line with no newline. One test writes 5000 bytes with no newline before the shell exits and checks all 5000 are kept.

Ways it differs from the model's bash tool (full list in the commit body):
• The leftover reader stops differently. The bash tool can abort its reader instantly. A plain thread can't be aborted, so mine is told to stop under a lock: nothing more is printed or stored after /run returns. The thread only closes its end of the pipe when the background job next writes or exits.
• Two small behaviour changes. Output that isn't valid UTF-8 is now decoded with replacement characters; the old loop stopped reading at the first bad line, which could stall a child that kept writing. And the dim note is new; the bash tool has none.
• Deliberately not copied: no process-group kill or timeout, and stdin is still inherited. /run runs in the foreground at your terminal, so Ctrl+C already reaches the child and interactive commands keep working.

Other checks before committing:
• Callers: no script or workflow in this repo runs yoyo run. The grep's one hit is prose in scripts/scan_commitments.py.
• Same bug elsewhere: /bg (src/commands_bg.rs:283-290) and the watch runner (src/watch.rs:1461-1499) also read to the end before waiting on the shell. I only read the code and didn't run either one. I filed both as #1063 and didn't fix them here.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md now says a backgrounded job keeps running, /run returns about 2s after the shell exits, and redirecting the job's output makes it return at once.
